%% First-boot cloud-init sequence (REPO mode) — installs clean, THEN re-applies config
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Boot as Target Boot
  participant Sub as Subiquity
  participant Guard as early-commands (guard)
  participant FS as fs layout
  participant CI as cloud-init (first boot)
  participant Apt as apt/snap/flatpak
  participant Ad as adapters (ollama, …)

  Boot->>Sub: kernel cmdline: autoinstall ds=nocloud-net;s=/wowiso/seed/
  Sub->>Guard: early-commands: compare live disk-id vs manifest.target_disk
  alt mismatch
    Guard-->>Sub: abort (no wipe)
  else match
    Guard-->>Sub: ok
    Sub->>FS: apply storage.layout (btrfs|f2fs), no encryption
    Sub->>Sub: install base system
    Sub->>CI: reboot into installed system
    CI->>Apt: add ppas/remotes, install packages.apt
    CI->>Apt: snap install …
    CI->>Apt: flatpak remote-add flathub; flatpak install …
    CI->>CI: restore /opt, ~/.config, .bashrc (perms/uid)
    CI->>Ad: for app in manifest.adapter_order:
    Ad->>Ad: install()   %% clean from repo
    Ad->>Ad: apply_config()  %% override.conf, OLLAMA_MODELS, shards as ollama:ollama
    Ad-->>CI: verify()  %% e.g. ollama list shows models
    CI-->>Boot: done — operator-ready
